Fix circular import between graph_tool.inference and graph_tool.draw.

base_states imports graph_tool.draw while graph_tool.inference is still being
initialized. graph_tool.draw imports symbols back from graph_tool.inference,
which causes a direct import of graph_tool.inference to fail with a partially
initialized module error. Import graph_tool.draw lazily in DrawBlockState.draw(),
where it is actually needed.

Author: Pavel Tomanek (Inuits/UGent) with help from ChatGPT5.6
--- a/src/graph_tool/inference/base_states.py
+++ b/src/graph_tool/inference/base_states.py
@@ -30,8 +30,6 @@
 import math
 import numpy
 
-import graph_tool.draw
-
 __test__ = False
 
 def set_test(test):
@@ -794,6 +792,7 @@
     def draw(self, **kwargs):
         r"""Convenience wrapper to :func:`~graph_tool.draw.graph_draw` that
         draws the state of the graph as colors on the vertices and edges."""
+        import graph_tool.draw
         gradient = self.g.new_ep("double")
         gradient = group_vector_property([gradient])
         b = self.g.own_property(self.b)
